But seriously, watch Mindy through this because she cannot face the scene.

1024
00:41:44.870 --> 00:41:45.410
It's amazing.

1025
00:41:45.910 --> 00:41:52.550
Well, when Rain grabs her and is like, all right, now from behind, she's like, wait, what?

1026
00:41:53.210 --> 00:41:53.650
Amazing.

1027
00:41:53.810 --> 00:41:55.010
I don't know how she got through that.

1028
00:41:55.150 --> 00:41:57.150
And there's all these great things in this.

1029
00:41:57.250 --> 00:42:00.950
This is the misuse of common phrases like catch 22.

1030
00:42:01.550 --> 00:42:02.510
Tit for tit.

1031
00:42:02.510 --> 00:42:03.570
That's your favorite.

1032
00:42:03.730 --> 00:42:04.070
My favorite.

1033
00:42:04.310 --> 00:42:06.110
This is the second time he has said it.

1034
00:42:06.410 --> 00:42:06.970
Tit for tit.

1035
00:42:07.650 --> 00:42:11.210
Also, two hits, me punching you and you hitting the floor.

1036
00:42:11.690 --> 00:42:13.030
It was so good.

1037
00:42:13.470 --> 00:42:14.950
It was just so good.

1038
00:42:15.190 --> 00:42:19.390
This leads me into my second time code, Angela.

1039
00:42:19.590 --> 00:42:19.890
Okay.

1040
00:42:20.710 --> 00:42:22.470
13 minutes, 27 seconds.

1041
00:42:22.930 --> 00:42:24.750
Well, I have one at 1325.

1042
00:42:25.130 --> 00:42:25.970
All right, what's yours?

1043
00:42:26.190 --> 00:42:26.530
Let's see.

1044
00:42:26.650 --> 00:42:28.030
Well, this is at 1325.

1045
00:42:28.030 --> 00:42:32.570
1325, you see who actually goes to the dojo because you see everyone pile into the elevator.

1046
00:42:32.830 --> 00:42:37.230
And it is Phyllis, Pam, Meredith, Oscar Creed, Kevin, Jim, Michael, and Dwight.

1047
00:42:37.230 --> 00:42:39.690
And who does not go to the dojo?

1048
00:42:40.410 --> 00:42:42.890
Angela, Stanley, Toby, Kelly, and Ryan.

1049
00:42:43.210 --> 00:42:44.130
Is that true?

1050
00:42:44.390 --> 00:42:44.470
Mm-hmm.

1051
00:42:44.670 --> 00:42:48.210
So you did not go to – did you not film that day when we went?

1052
00:42:48.210 --> 00:42:49.810
I had the day off.

1053
00:42:50.110 --> 00:42:51.310
Oh, my gosh.

1054
00:42:51.310 --> 00:42:53.190
Yeah, it was decadent.

1055
00:42:53.450 --> 00:42:54.550
It was decadent.

1056
00:42:54.670 --> 00:42:54.850
Oh, my goodness.

1057
00:42:54.990 --> 00:42:59.030
So when I talk about being at the dojo, you're going to hear what you missed out on.

1058
00:42:59.110 --> 00:43:00.250
Yeah, I have no idea.

1059
00:43:00.470 --> 00:43:05.370
And, you know, the thinking was that Angela and Stanley would not participate in this.

1060
00:43:05.470 --> 00:43:06.770
This is like shenanigans.

1061
00:43:06.770 --> 00:43:10.010
And they are literally there to do work and clock in and clock out.

1062
00:43:10.190 --> 00:43:10.390
Yes.

1063
00:43:10.630 --> 00:43:15.010
And so Angela and Stanley are really two of the big bah humbugs of the office.

1064
00:43:15.370 --> 00:43:20.270
Toby and Kelly wouldn't go or Ryan because, as you know and I know, they were writers.

1065
00:43:20.270 --> 00:43:22.130
And they needed to be in the writer's room.

1066
00:43:22.230 --> 00:43:24.590
And this was an opportunity for them to get some work done.

1067
00:43:24.910 --> 00:43:26.190
Yes, it's so true.

1068
00:43:26.610 --> 00:43:30.890
Well, when we all pile in the elevator, I don't know why I'm so tickled by it.

1069
00:43:30.990 --> 00:43:36.510
But at 13 minutes and 27 seconds, just watch Kevin's face as the elevator doors close.

1070
00:43:36.870 --> 00:43:37.270
Okay.

1071
00:43:37.630 --> 00:43:38.650
It just makes me laugh.

1072
00:43:38.770 --> 00:43:39.130
All right.

1073
00:43:39.210 --> 00:43:41.310
He's got this little mischievous look on his face.

1074
00:43:41.450 --> 00:43:43.790
Like, he's very excited to see what's going to happen.

1075
00:43:44.090 --> 00:43:46.470
Totally like a little kid who got to leave school.

1076
00:43:46.690 --> 00:43:47.610
Oh, that's so cute.

1077
00:43:47.650 --> 00:43:48.230
I love it.

1078
00:43:48.230 --> 00:43:48.590
All right.

1079
00:43:48.710 --> 00:43:51.110
Well, Angela, I'm going to tell you some stuff.

1080
00:43:51.850 --> 00:43:56.670
The day that we shot at the dojo, it was really hot.

1081
00:43:56.850 --> 00:43:59.070
I was going to say, were you guys all hot and sweaty?

1082
00:43:59.310 --> 00:43:59.730
Yes.

1083
00:43:59.870 --> 00:44:02.950
And the air conditioning in our trailers wasn't working.

1084
00:44:03.190 --> 00:44:03.510
Oh.

1085
00:44:03.770 --> 00:44:06.450
So remember on the dundies when they had ants?

1086
00:44:06.690 --> 00:44:09.410
This time, they had no air conditioning.

1087
00:44:09.750 --> 00:44:11.650
And they were, they're metal.

1088
00:44:12.130 --> 00:44:15.210
So it was kind of like changing your clothes in a sauna.

1089
00:44:15.610 --> 00:44:19.930
And we were just super sweaty, all of us, and gross.

1090
00:44:20.310 --> 00:44:22.230
And I had to wear a sweater.

1091
00:44:22.450 --> 00:44:22.670
Yeah.

1092
00:44:22.810 --> 00:44:25.950
Because we had established my beige sweater earlier in the office.

1093
00:44:25.950 --> 00:44:31.490
And I remember thinking, oh, my God, I am so sweaty and stinky.

1094
00:44:31.710 --> 00:44:34.330
And John has to pick me up.

1095
00:44:34.330 --> 00:44:39.130
This is, this is a thing that I think people don't think about.

1096
00:44:39.610 --> 00:44:49.230
You know, anytime I would have a scene where I would have to whisper at someone or you'd have to kiss, I would brush my teeth like three times and chew gum and eat a mint before.

1097
00:44:49.230 --> 00:44:56.350
And anytime when you have to be close to someone, I would be very aware of my potential body odor.

1098
00:44:57.370 --> 00:45:00.590
At least our show wasn't a show with a bunch of close talkers.

1099
00:45:00.710 --> 00:45:03.190
Because, like, you watch an episode of, like, The Sopranos.

1100
00:45:03.230 --> 00:45:04.490
They get in each other's faces.

1101
00:45:04.490 --> 00:45:05.570
They're like, listen here.

1102
00:45:05.830 --> 00:45:07.630
And they're, like, right up to each other's face.

1103
00:45:07.730 --> 00:45:09.010
Like, at least we didn't have that.

1104
00:45:09.190 --> 00:45:09.710
That's true.

1105
00:45:09.770 --> 00:45:17.630
But when I watch those scenes, because we're actors and we know, I think, like, oh, my God, there's no way they don't know what they had for lunch.

1106
00:45:17.630 --> 00:45:19.370
Because that is some close talking.

1107
00:45:19.790 --> 00:45:22.410
Well, when Jim lifts Pam up at the dojo.

1108
00:45:22.610 --> 00:45:24.470
At 14 minutes, 11 seconds.

1109
00:45:24.530 --> 00:45:27.190
We got a lot of questions about this scene.

1110
00:45:27.350 --> 00:45:28.950
I have questions, so go.

1111
00:45:29.430 --> 00:45:33.550
Well, in Office Olympics, Angela has her bit about Pam Pong.

1112
00:45:33.710 --> 00:45:34.090
Yes.

1113
00:45:34.270 --> 00:45:39.750
And that's kind of the first time that Pam is made aware that someone else is aware.

1114
00:45:39.970 --> 00:45:41.050
People are noticing.

1115
00:45:41.330 --> 00:45:41.630
Yes.

1116
00:45:41.630 --> 00:45:51.250
And now, in this scene, Meredith clocks the interaction between Pam and Jim, and that is what freaks out Pam.

1117
00:45:51.530 --> 00:45:53.990
Also, your shirt came up, and you could see your belly.

1118
00:45:54.190 --> 00:46:01.570
Now, I remember as your friend that week, you saying to me, oh, my gosh, oh, my gosh, people are going to see my belly.

1119
00:46:01.790 --> 00:46:05.470
Because it said, you know, it picks up and your shirt kind of comes up, and you were nervous about it.

1120
00:46:05.470 --> 00:46:08.330
Yeah, that was all, that was, so that was a fan question.

1121
00:46:08.510 --> 00:46:14.130
Anthony asked, was it meant for your shirt to pull up when Jim lifted you, or did it happen on accident and you went with it?

1122
00:46:14.270 --> 00:46:23.770
It was in the script that my shirt would come up a little bit, and that was all to make it even more of a vulnerable thing for Pam.

1123
00:46:23.950 --> 00:46:26.090
That she was literally exposed.

1124
00:46:26.450 --> 00:46:28.630
Yeah, something that you were really embarrassed about.

1125
00:46:28.630 --> 00:46:32.130
Yes, and wow, I wish my stomach looked like that today.

1126
00:46:32.690 --> 00:46:40.990
I watched that scene, and I was like, why was I not wearing midriff tops every day when I looked like that?

1127
00:46:41.210 --> 00:46:48.710
I know, I knew you were going to say that, because, I mean, listen, we've had babies, and everything changes after that.

1128
00:46:48.850 --> 00:46:51.330
And you're, I mean, you look phenomenal today, Jenna.

1129
00:46:51.450 --> 00:46:52.410
You look phenomenal then.

1130
00:46:52.530 --> 00:46:55.670
But I know, I remember our bellies before babies.

1131
00:46:55.670 --> 00:46:56.290
I remember.

1132
00:46:56.290 --> 00:47:07.510
Well, I am kind of glad that it was scripted that you see my belly, because I've got it on film now, that at one time in my life, I had a cute little belly and belly button.

1133
00:47:07.770 --> 00:47:09.890
So, thank you, Jean and Lee, for that.

1134
00:47:10.590 --> 00:47:20.110
At 13 minutes, 56 seconds, that's my third time code, Angela, there is a poster in the background of this interaction between Jim and Pam.

1135
00:47:20.110 --> 00:47:27.490
So, we're all watching Jim and Pam, but in the background, there is a poster on the wall, and it is one of my favorite things.

1136
00:47:27.630 --> 00:47:31.230
It was, like, a favorite thing of all of us when we got to the dojo.

1137
00:47:31.350 --> 00:47:38.490
This was a set decoration poster that Jean and Lee wrote that set decoration had printed and put on the wall.

1138
00:47:38.550 --> 00:47:41.250
It is the Ten Rules of Karate.

1139
00:47:41.550 --> 00:47:41.970
Okay.

1140
00:47:41.970 --> 00:47:46.490
All right, according to this dojo, and I'm going to read them to you.

1141
00:47:46.570 --> 00:47:46.830
Okay.

1142
00:47:47.290 --> 00:47:47.990
They're amazing.

1143
00:47:48.650 --> 00:47:50.910
Number one, obey your parents.

1144
00:47:51.250 --> 00:47:51.710
Okay.

1145
00:47:51.930 --> 00:47:53.990
Number two, no junk food.

1146
00:47:54.450 --> 00:47:56.650
Number three, do your homework.

1147
00:47:57.350 --> 00:47:59.710
Number four, keep your room clean.

1148
00:48:00.190 --> 00:48:03.290
Number five, maintain an indomitable spirit.

1149
00:48:03.930 --> 00:48:06.370
Number six, don't fight with your siblings.

1150
00:48:07.010 --> 00:48:10.170
Seven, practice, practice, practice.

1151
00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:14.010
Eight, treat others the way you would like to be treated.

1152
00:48:14.850 --> 00:48:16.750
Nine, be loyal to your country.

1153
00:48:17.070 --> 00:48:18.810
And ten, have fun.

1154
00:48:19.510 --> 00:48:22.410
So, Lee told me he still has this poster.

1155
00:48:22.550 --> 00:48:23.390
He asked to have it.

1156
00:48:23.510 --> 00:48:26.350
He said they spent way too long writing these tools.

1157
00:48:26.350 --> 00:48:28.490
I was going to say, I bet they spent, like, hours.

1158
00:48:28.730 --> 00:48:29.530
They did.

1159
00:48:29.730 --> 00:48:30.970
Like, cracking themselves up.

1160
00:48:30.970 --> 00:48:40.290
It's amazing to me because I feel like it is this little detail that really hammers home that Dwight takes classes in a studio meant for children.

1161
00:48:40.710 --> 00:48:41.850
Children, do your homework.

1162
00:48:42.050 --> 00:48:43.790
These are kid-based rules.

1163
00:48:43.970 --> 00:48:44.170
Yeah.

1164
00:48:44.370 --> 00:48:45.810
And, of course, you see that.

1165
00:48:45.930 --> 00:48:48.690
You see that he's in a class with a bunch of 11-year-olds.

1166
00:48:48.690 --> 00:48:51.950
But I just think that is brilliant.

1167
00:48:52.130 --> 00:48:53.530
Brilliant writing, that poster.

1168
00:48:53.930 --> 00:48:57.850
Okay, so that was their version of the rules of karate, right?

1169
00:48:57.850 --> 00:49:00.030
Yeah, there's this thread on Reddit where people go back and forth.

1170
00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:03.670
They were like, but Dwight says karate, and then there's taekwondo this, and there's this and this.

1171
00:49:03.770 --> 00:49:07.310
So, a little bit that the martial arts didn't quite line up in that dojo.

1172
00:49:07.630 --> 00:49:10.010
Yeah, I think that makes sense, too.

1173
00:49:10.230 --> 00:49:16.250
I mean, Dwight is not maybe studying a pure form of any one martial art.

1174
00:49:16.450 --> 00:49:16.730
Right.

1175
00:49:17.070 --> 00:49:23.470
I have to talk about the fact that at 14 minutes, 11 seconds, I think that Pam is sending Jim mixed signals.

1176
00:49:24.030 --> 00:49:24.890
Of course she is.

1177
00:49:24.890 --> 00:49:26.690
And I totally judged her a little bit.

1178
00:49:26.810 --> 00:49:27.170
I know.

1179
00:49:27.170 --> 00:49:28.770
Because she was being really flirty.

1180
00:49:28.890 --> 00:49:33.350
And then when Meredith noticed, it wasn't until Meredith noticed.

1181
00:49:33.350 --> 00:49:33.830
That's right.

1182
00:49:33.990 --> 00:49:35.690
That then she, like, pushed Jim away.

1183
00:49:35.690 --> 00:49:43.890
And then the look on John's face, he does such a fantastic job of looking wounded and confused and not really.

1184
00:49:44.010 --> 00:49:46.530
He was so happy, but now he's like, now what happened?

1185
00:49:47.050 --> 00:49:47.350
Yeah.

1186
00:49:47.650 --> 00:49:51.010
He did such a great job because Pam is sending him mixed signals.

1187
00:49:51.210 --> 00:49:51.990
She really is.

1188
00:49:52.110 --> 00:49:55.350
But, I mean, that's complicated, unrequited love for you.

1189
00:49:55.510 --> 00:49:55.950
I know.

1190
00:49:57.170 --> 00:49:58.270
She's conflicted.

1191
00:49:58.390 --> 00:49:59.350
She's conflicted.

1192
00:49:59.350 --> 00:50:09.270
When Michael pins down Dwight at the dojo and is winning the fight, our director of photography, Randall Einhorn, who used to work on Survivor.

1193
00:50:09.350 --> 00:50:12.450
So I want to say, literally nothing surprises this man.

1194
00:50:12.450 --> 00:50:13.350
He is a total pro.

1195
00:50:13.550 --> 00:50:14.310
He never broke.

1196
00:50:14.670 --> 00:50:16.350
He lost it.

1197
00:50:16.350 --> 00:50:24.990
He was laughing so hard that he had to take the camera off his shoulder and hold it out with his arm so that it wouldn't shake.

1198
00:50:25.270 --> 00:50:29.030
He had tears, like, streaming down his face.

1199
00:50:29.770 --> 00:50:31.510
It's the hardest I've ever seen him laugh.

1200
00:50:31.790 --> 00:50:32.150
Yeah.

1201
00:50:32.350 --> 00:50:34.630
That's saying something because he was like a statue.

1202
00:50:34.830 --> 00:50:36.790
Him and Oscar Nunez never break.

1203
00:50:36.990 --> 00:50:37.150
Yeah.

1204
00:50:37.370 --> 00:50:38.510
I have a question for you.

1205
00:50:38.670 --> 00:50:45.610
Lance, when I was speaking to him, said to his knowledge the fight was not choreographed and that he really believed that the stuff that Michael,

1206
00:50:45.910 --> 00:50:52.930
that Steve was doing to Rain as Dwight, like holding him down and trying to spit on him and all of that, that Steve improvised that.

1207
00:50:52.930 --> 00:50:54.750
I asked Lee about that.

1208
00:50:54.950 --> 00:51:01.070
His memory is that they did bring in a stunt coordinator to work with them on set one day during a break.

1209
00:51:01.290 --> 00:51:01.450
Yeah.

1210
00:51:01.570 --> 00:51:02.970
So Lance wouldn't have been there for that.

1211
00:51:03.130 --> 00:51:03.650
That's right.

1212
00:51:03.850 --> 00:51:04.350
And so.

1213
00:51:04.750 --> 00:51:06.830
But that person did not go to the dojo.

1214
00:51:07.090 --> 00:51:07.490
Did not go to the dojo.

1215
00:51:07.510 --> 00:51:09.990
The day that you actually did it, they were not present.

1216
00:51:10.290 --> 00:51:18.430
And so on the day, he said they just, like, Steve and Rain and Ken Kwapis just came up with a bunch of stuff, like the typewriter stuff.

1217
00:51:18.430 --> 00:51:22.790
And just, he said, he doesn't remember how many takes they did, but it was a lot.

1218
00:51:22.910 --> 00:51:24.590
But he said it was also really hot.

1219
00:51:24.710 --> 00:51:27.690
And those guys got really tired doing all the fake fighting.

1220
00:51:27.950 --> 00:51:30.770
You can tell because they're winded when they're speaking to each other.

1221
00:51:31.170 --> 00:51:31.850
They are.

1222
00:51:32.410 --> 00:51:33.210
It's true.

1223
00:51:33.750 --> 00:51:40.270
Did you clock Phyllis's disposable camera in the scene where she's taking pictures and it's a disposable camera?

1224
00:51:40.270 --> 00:51:41.650
Don't you wish we had those pictures?

1225
00:51:41.810 --> 00:51:42.510
Who has those?

1226
00:51:42.750 --> 00:51:43.470
Someone muSt.

1227
00:51:43.610 --> 00:51:43.810
Yeah.

1228
00:51:44.010 --> 00:51:44.570
Phil Shea?

1229
00:51:44.770 --> 00:51:45.230
Phil Shea.

1230
00:51:48.430 --> 00:51:49.270
It's a devastating defeat.

1231
00:51:49.630 --> 00:51:59.950
We go back to the office and we see a scene from Michael's office that goes down into the parking lot and he tries to call Ryan on his cell phone.

1232
00:52:00.350 --> 00:52:03.970
That was a different office than the usual Michael's office.

1233
00:52:04.170 --> 00:52:06.590
You totally, like, it's completely different.

1234
00:52:06.890 --> 00:52:07.150
Yes.

1235
00:52:07.270 --> 00:52:09.210
So we had two Michael's offices.

1236
00:52:09.490 --> 00:52:11.910
We had one Michael's office that was on our set.

1237
00:52:11.910 --> 00:52:22.650
And it had just like a scrim backdrop behind the window that was kind of blurry and it was just old-fashioned fake out the window kind of thing.

1238
00:52:23.170 --> 00:52:31.170
But whenever we had to shoot a scene where Michael was actually looking out of his window into the parking lot, we would move over to the writer's offices.

1239
00:52:31.430 --> 00:52:34.110
And they literally would shoot in a writer's office.

1240
00:52:34.330 --> 00:52:34.610
Yes.

1241
00:52:34.610 --> 00:52:39.730
And I was trying to remember, was it Mike Schur's office or Paul Lieberstein's office?

1242
00:52:40.050 --> 00:52:44.590
They, one of the two of them worked in Michael's office.

1243
00:52:44.850 --> 00:52:44.950
Right.

1244
00:52:44.950 --> 00:52:47.330
And it was loosely decorated as Michael's office.

1245
00:52:47.430 --> 00:52:53.150
And then when it was time to shoot, they would get kicked out of their office and set dressing would come in and zhuzh it up.

1246
00:52:53.270 --> 00:52:53.550
Mm-hmm.

1247
00:52:53.670 --> 00:52:57.450
And then they would have to use that to shoot and they couldn't write in their office that day.

1248
00:52:57.590 --> 00:53:00.110
But the walls are like kind of a green color.

1249
00:53:00.250 --> 00:53:00.510
Yes.

1250
00:53:00.650 --> 00:53:01.690
That was always true.

1251
00:53:01.690 --> 00:53:02.030
That don't match.

1252
00:53:02.170 --> 00:53:03.330
That don't match.

1253
00:53:03.450 --> 00:53:05.790
Like, I was like, guys, the walls are not the same.

1254
00:53:06.030 --> 00:53:10.050
Well, it's funny, too, because all the other writers could decorate their offices.

1255
00:53:10.310 --> 00:53:11.890
Oh, Mindy's office was so decorated.

1256
00:53:12.130 --> 00:53:12.470
Oh, for sure.

1257
